  "id": "central-tendency",
  "term": "central tendency",
  "definition": "In time perception, central tendency is the pattern in which judgments are drawn toward a central or average value. Its size varies across people and is linked to timing precision, with noisier internal representations tending to produce a stronger central tendency.",
